{
  "$comment": [
    "Golden vectors for the DIG mirror-coin collateral recurrence, transcribed from the",
    "normative decision on DIG-Network/dig_ecosystem#3173, section 13, under protocol version 1.",
    "",
    "This file is the cross-language conformance contract: a second implementation in any",
    "language must reproduce every field below byte-identically from the census inputs alone.",
    "It is data rather than inline assertions precisely so it can be consumed elsewhere.",
    "",
    "All amounts are DIG base units; 1 DIG = 1_000 DIG base units, so the smallest expressible",
    "amount is 0.001 DIG. A DIG base unit is never a mojo: a mojo is XCH's base unit,",
    "10^-12 XCH, nine orders of magnitude away.",
    "All *_micros fields are fixed-point with 1_000_000 == 1.0.",
    "",
    "`posted_each` is what an operator at the 1% default safety margin would post for this",
    "epoch's requirement, i.e. ceil(required(n) * 101 / 100). It is what produces the next",
    "epoch's `locked`, and it is not consensus.",
    "",
    "Epoch 1 is the bootstrap anchor: no census precedes it, so its signals and band are null.",
    "Epoch 8 is the designed shock: counted advertisements fall 74 -> 33, a 55% collapse.",
    "",
    "These vectors are the conformance contract for PROTOCOL VERSION 1 specifically. They are",
    "kept and keep running after a later version activates: a retired ruleset's vectors are the",
    "regression test that a refactor did not quietly rewrite history."
  ],
